+---
+type: adr
+status: stable
+entities: [Post]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Controllers/HomeController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/PostResource.ts
+  - app/Http/Validators/PostValidator.ts
+  - app/Console/Commands/PostsScheduledCommand.ts
+  - bin/console.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-fable/5.1", at: 2026-09-25T06:31:02.980Z }
+---
+
+# Schedule posts with a nullable published_at timestamp
+
+## Context
+
+Authors write ahead of time, but a post went live the moment it was saved,
+so launches were kept in a spreadsheet and pasted in by hand. We need
+"write now, publish later" without a scheduler process or a publish button.
+
+## Decision
+
+- `posts.published_at` is a nullable ISO 8601 UTC text column, stored the
+  same way as `created_at`. `NULL` or a past instant means public; a future
+  instant means scheduled. Nothing flips at publish time: visibility is
+  computed against the current instant on every read, so the post becomes
+  public with no further action.
+- The form field is `publishAt` on `posts.store` and `posts.update`
+  (optional, `null` = publish now). It is validated as an ISO 8601 date and
+  time with a zone offset and normalized to UTC before it is stored.
+- Visibility is one rule in [Post](../../app/Models/Post.ts):
+  `isVisibleTo()` for a single record and `visibleTo()` as the matching
+  where-group for list, search and home queries. A scheduled post is
+  visible to its author only; everyone else gets a 404 on its page and
+  never sees it in lists or search.
+- `bun run console posts:scheduled` prints `<id>\t<title>\t<published_at>`
+  per scheduled post, soonest first, and nothing else on stdout so it can
+  be piped. `bin/console.ts` routes boot notices to stderr for that reason.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- No cron, queue or "publish" action is needed, and clocks are compared as
+  ISO text, which only stays correct while every writer stores UTC with the
+  same `toISOString()` shape. Moving `published_at` into the past directly in
+  the database is a supported way to publish early.
+- Unpublishing a live post means giving it a future date; there is no
+  separate draft state.
+- Every read path that lists posts must apply `Post.visibleTo()`; a new
+  query that forgets it leaks scheduled posts.
